# superpowers plan workspaces (ledger, briefs, review packages — scratch only)
.superpowers/

# ── Nested admin deployment ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sarvadnya-advanced is the ADMIN deployment fork of this repo
# (origin: ankit-sarvadnya/advanced-sarvadnya.git). It lives here as a
# standalone git repository so admin work can be done in the same context,
# but it is NOT part of this repository.
#
# It is IGNORED, not a submodule. A submodule would make this repo hold a
# gitlink (mode 160000) pointing at an admin-fork commit; a stray `git add -A`
# would otherwise publish that reference into the public frontend repo.
#
# Its own .gitignore handles .env*, node_modules and .next inside it, so those
# never leak here either. See tsconfig.json "exclude" for the matching entry —
# without it `tsc --noEmit` pulls all 167 of its files into this repo's
# typecheck and resolves their "@/..." imports against THIS root.
# CHANGE: 2026-10-02 — nested advanced-sarvadnya admin deployment, see
# docs/NESTED-ADMIN-REPO.md and AGENTS.md §10.
/sarvadnya-advanced/

# CHANGE: 2026-10-02 — scripts/excel-log-append.mjs writes a pre-append backup next to the
# CSV on every run. It is a runtime artifact of that one script, not project data, and was
# previously untracked-but-not-ignored, so it would have been swept into a commit by `git add -A`.
# CHANGE: 2026-10-02 — scripts/db-backup.mjs writes timestamped JSON dumps of the
# shared Atlas database here. Runtime artifacts, never committed (restore from a
# downloaded/copied copy; a push must not sweep production data into the repo).
/backups/

# CHANGE: 2026-10-02 — scripts/excel-log-append.mjs writes a pre-append backup next to the
# CSV on every run. It is a runtime artifact of that one script, not project data, and was
# previously untracked-but-not-ignored, so it would have been swept into a commit by `git add -A`.
*.csv.bak

# CHANGE: 2026-10-03 — non-served brand master assets (3500x3500 logo master etc.).
# public/logo.png is the web-optimized serving copy; the full-res master lives here
# (gitignored so the 5.4 MB art file never enters the repo) per owner: "keep new logo — optimize it".
brand-assets/
